  pooled padding: left median 0, right median 0, max |pad| 6116

Read this as the specification for sim/window.py: the curated window is
the event span plus a small constant (per type: ES +100 bp on each edge,
IR exactly 0, A3/A5 -1 -- an off-by-one coordinate convention). Drawing a
label-independent flank of the same magnitude reproduces the geometry
without hard-coding a per-class constant, which would be pure leakage.
